WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.340
Sunburn.

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:02.440
Seagulls.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.760
Knife-wielding crabs.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.899
Three very good reasons to spend absolutely
no time outside this summer.

00:00:07.899 --> 00:00:12.780
Thankfully, there are at least seventeen more
excellent reasons to cancel your beach plans

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:13.780
this year.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.630
Eighteen if you count the fact that you'll
definitely get sand in your bathing suit area.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.230
The summer of 2017 has some must-sees for
anybody's list, so butter up your popcorn

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:27.170
and let's get your butt-meats in the theater
seats for these blockbuster films.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.269
Pirates of the Caribbean: Dead Men Tell No
Tales

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:35.000
We're four films deep into the Pirates of
the Caribbean franchise, and Johnny Depp's

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.750
Captain Jack Sparrow is still swashbuckling
his way across the seven seas.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.160
The newest installment, Dead Men Tell No Tales,
will bring us one film deeper.

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.670
This time, the race is on to find the Trident
of Poseidon, which gives its owner complete

00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.600
power over the seas.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:56.470
The notoriously creepy Javier Bardem appears
as Jack's undead nemesis, and franchise favorites

00:00:56.470 --> 00:01:00.870
Orlando Bloom and Geoffrey Rush are making
a return to the series once more.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:06.200
Also, watch out for a cameo by Paul McCartney
in his second weirdest nautical film role

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.700
when the film is released on May 26th.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.780
Baywatch

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:14.700
Let's be totally honest: no one ever watched
Baywatch in the '90s for its stimulating plot.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:20.020
No, it was mostly for the totally wicked Hulk
Hogan jet ski accidents.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.160
"Whooa, ohhhh, ah!

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:28.040
Ohhhhh, ah...oh!"

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:34.240
Now, the TV hit best known for its red swimsuits
and slow motion running is back, this time

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:35.520
as a big-screen comedy.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.810
Hey, it worked for 21 Jump Street, right?

00:01:39.080 --> 00:01:40.380
"My name is Jeff."

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:45.420
Starring Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson and Zac
Efron as lifeguards who have to stop a criminal

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:51.700
mastermind, and with cameos by original Baywatch
stars Pamela Anderson and David Hasselhoff,

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.219
this film looks like a pretty good way to
start your summer.

00:01:54.219 --> 00:01:56.810
Hit the beach on May 26th.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:57.959
Wonder Woman

00:01:57.959 --> 00:02:04.040
On June 2nd, Wonder Woman finally gets a film
of her own… and it only took like 76 years.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:09.280
Seriously, how many Batman and Superman movies
do we need before a lady finally gets a break?

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:14.280
A far cry from the spinning Wonder Woman of
the '70s, Gal Gadot's turn as the superhero

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:18.380
has already proven that she can kick some
butt and use her lasso like a boss.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:24.360
Now, her solo film explores her Amazonian
origins, and life during World War I. Plus,

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:28.830
Chris Pine has a history of making new franchises
great, so his place in the cast is a great

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:29.320
sign.

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:29.980
The Mummy

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.440
Welcome to the Universal Cinematic Universe.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.480
The….

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.970
Universal Universe.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.170
The Cinematic Universal?

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.530
Actually, we're not totally sure what they're
calling it yet.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:44.870
On June 9th, Universal is getting into the
universe-building game, creating a coherent

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:49.120
collection of movies from its classic monsters,
beginning with The Mummy.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:53.990
Frankenstein's monster, the Invisible Man,
the Creature from the Black Lagoon, and probably

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:59.320
a Dracula or two will eventually come together
to do whatever it is that monsters do — and

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:00.650
it all starts this summer.

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:05.090
Tom Cruise is a fantastic choice to lead a
new action universe, and this film will feature

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:10.040
the first character crossover with Russell
Crowe playing Dr. Jekyll, signalling a whole

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:11.930
monstrous world to come.

00:03:11.930 --> 00:03:15.960
Hopefully this song will play over the end-credits
of every one of these movies:

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:16.860
"They did the mash."

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.940
"They did the monnnster mash."

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.100
"The monster mash."

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:22.370
Cars 3

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:28.150
When the first teaser for Pixar's Cars 3 basically
featured hero Lightning McQueen getting slow-motion

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:32.510
murdered by an accident on the track, you
know you're in for a very weird ride.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:37.460
The Cars franchise is getting into some pretty
unexpected stuff, especially considering Cars

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:39.810
2 focused on 'Mater becoming a spy.

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:44.150
Who could possibly be prepared for the dark
intensity of Cars 3?

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:48.590
Not the hundreds of crying children who just
saw their hero's body parts flying in every

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:49.590
direction.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:53.230
The film deals with Lightning McQueen getting
aged out of his sport and trying to win back

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:58.440
acclaim from the younger, faster cars... which
sounds like some pretty heavy stuff.

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:03.850
The original voice cast returns on June 16th,
alongside Armie Hammer, Nathan Fillion, and

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:05.070
Kerry Washington.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:07.030
Get ready to feel old.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:09.510
Transformers: The Last Knight

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:13.460
When you hear Michael Bay, you think one thing:
explosions.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:15.620
"Michael Bay...splosions!"

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:23.340
On the tenth anniversary of the start of Michael
Bay's Transformers franchise, we get his fifth

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:26.830
installment about shape-changing alien robots.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.099
Don't take the "Last" in The Last Knight too
literally, though.

00:04:30.099 --> 00:04:35.120
Bay said it may be his last film, but Paramount
is definitely making a Bumblebee movie and

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:39.639
will probably crank out more Transformers
as long as the box office receipts keep rolling

00:04:39.639 --> 00:04:41.300
in and the action figures keep selling.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.160
"Optimus Prime is lagging!

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.660
Catch up with Soundwave!

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:45.860
Robots in disguise!"

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:52.280
In The Last Knight, Optimus Prime isn't exactly
around, and it's up to puny humans Mark Wahlberg,

00:04:52.289 --> 00:04:56.030
Anthony Hopkins, and Stanley Tucci to save
the world from evil 'bots.

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:59.970
The film won't suffer from any shortage of
action and explosions.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:01.870
Because, you know, Michael Bay.

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:05.419
"Hi I'm Michael Bay, director of Hollywood
hits such as Transformers.

00:05:05.419 --> 00:05:07.150
And I demand things to be awesome.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.569
Awesome pussy cat.

00:05:08.569 --> 00:05:10.069
Awesome barbecue.

00:05:10.069 --> 00:05:11.580
Awesome pool."

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:16.050
And there's even a badass girl fighter, if
you didn't get enough of that in Logan.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.449
Transform and roll out on June 23rd.

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:19.449
Baby Driver

00:05:19.449 --> 00:05:24.280
Director Edgar Wright described his newest
film, Baby Driver, as "a car movie fueled

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:25.520
by music."

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:29.930
It looks like a huge departure from his usual
fare, which includes Shaun of the Dead, Hot

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:32.960
Fuzz, and Scott Pilgrim vs. the World.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:38.280
Starring Ansel Elgort, Kevin Spacey, Jamie
Foxx, and Jon Hamm, Baby Driver crashes into

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:41.740
theaters on June 28th, just a few weeks ahead
of schedule.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.850
Despicable Me 3

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:49.370
We get double the Steve Carell in Despicable
Me's latest sequel when Gru finds his long-lost,

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:53.900
long-haired twin brother, Dru, who convinces
him to return to his evil ways for just one

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:54.900
last heist.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.909
And as always, there's going to be plenty
of Minions, because that never gets old.

00:05:58.909 --> 00:05:59.909
Never.

00:05:59.909 --> 00:06:04.319
For real, prepare for a whole new wave of
terrible Minion memes from your troubled Aunt

00:06:04.319 --> 00:06:06.210
Gloria on Facebook.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:10.050
In this third installment, cartoon mayhem
is pretty much guaranteed.

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:15.349
Kristen Wiig returns, joined by Jenny Slate,
and Trey Parker making a rare, non-South Park

00:06:15.349 --> 00:06:16.889
voice appearance.

00:06:16.889 --> 00:06:19.610
Prepare for supervillainy on June 30th.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:22.979
Steve Carell hasn't had such an entertaining
twin since Prison Mike.

00:06:22.979 --> 00:06:26.229
"The worst thing about prison was the...was
the dementors!

00:06:26.229 --> 00:06:30.689
They...were flying all over the place and
they were scary and then they'd come down

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:33.460
and they'd suck the soul outta ya body and
it hoit!"

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:34.830
Spider-Man: Homecoming

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:40.620
We may be onto our third version of Spider-Man
since 2002, but we're excited to see how Tom

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:45.469
Holland handles his own picture after his
Peter Parker stole the show in Captain America:

00:06:45.469 --> 00:06:46.469
Civil War.

00:06:46.469 --> 00:06:51.210
So far, Holland has given the character his
own spin while remaining true to the Spidey

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.829
that we all know and love.

00:06:52.829 --> 00:06:57.919
With Robert Downey Jr. crossing over as Tony
Stark, and Michael Keaton as The Vulture,

00:06:57.920 --> 00:07:01.100
we can't wait to witness Spider-Man 3.0 on
July 7th.

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.620
War for the Planet of the Apes

00:07:06.639 --> 00:07:12.750
Monkeys and humans have been at war for hundreds
of years — but this time, it's serious.

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:17.560
Caesar rides again in War for the Planet of
the Apes on July 14th, and now, he's on a

00:07:17.560 --> 00:07:19.629
quest for vengeance.

00:07:19.629 --> 00:07:24.009
Woody Harrelson stars as the vicious Colonel,
the leader of the human army, and director

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:26.349
Matt Reeves returns to the helm once again.

00:07:26.349 --> 00:07:31.129
Though it might seem that this war would conclude
the Planet of the Apes story, Reeves and producer

00:07:31.129 --> 00:07:35.129
Dylan Clark say there will be room for plenty
more Apes stories to come.

00:07:35.129 --> 00:07:36.810
Hopefully, at least one of them will be a
musical.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:45.619
"I hate every ape I see, from chimpan-A to
chimpanzee."

00:07:45.619 --> 00:07:46.619
Dunkirk

00:07:46.619 --> 00:07:52.259
It's true: there's at least one big film this
summer that isn't a remake, reboot, or sequel.

00:07:52.259 --> 00:07:56.280
Okay, yes, there was a movie called Dunkirk
in 1958.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:08:00.340
But this summer's version is all new, and
comes from an original script by Christopher

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:03.819
Nolan, who's taking a break from sci-fi fantasy
fare.

00:08:03.819 --> 00:08:08.940
Nolan will also direct, with Dark Knight alums
Tom Hardy and Cillian Murphy starring, as

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:12.089
well as Kenneth Branagh, and Mark Rylance.

00:08:12.089 --> 00:08:17.460
It's the true tale of a difficult evacuation
of Allied soldiers from the beaches of Dunkirk,

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:18.460
France.

00:08:18.460 --> 00:08:23.080
This historical action-drama, filmed on location,
seems like a great palate cleanser from the

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:25.199
rest of summer's fantasy fare.

00:08:25.199 --> 00:08:29.270
You know, if you like to cleanse your palate
with the horrors of war.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:32.080
Check it out on July 21st.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:34.550
Valerian and the City of a Thousand Planets

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:39.660
Luc Besson, the guy who gifted the world with
Milla Jovovich in thermal bandages in The

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:43.700
Fifth Element, is here to bring us another
future-set action/adventure.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:48.399
Based on the French sci-fi comic series Valérian
and Laureline, the film is about a peaceful

00:08:48.399 --> 00:08:51.070
civilization threatened with a great evil.

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:55.210
Time-traveling special ops heroes Valerian
and Laureline are there to stop it.

00:08:55.210 --> 00:08:59.100
World-building, ingenious aliens, and… shapeshifting
Rihanna?

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.899
Yes, this movie has it all.

00:09:00.899 --> 00:09:05.930
Besson knows how to make futuristic sci-fi,
and Valerian seems to be no exception.

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:09.190
Get ready to save the universe on July 21st.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.190
The Emoji Movie

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:14.449
"It's my pleasure to announce our first movie.

00:09:14.449 --> 00:09:15.860
Yay."

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:22.340
Sure, making a film based on instant messaging
symbols may sound odd, but with a pretty solid

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:26.490
voice cast, director Tony Leondis has figured
out a way to make it work.

00:09:26.490 --> 00:09:27.490
Probably.

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:32.900
Legendary comedian Steven Wright, who has
always been the living, breathing Meh emoji,

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:34.730
is just one of the many inspired castings.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:39.470
"Last night I stayed up all night playing
poker with Tarot cards.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:44.250
Got a full house and four people died."

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:49.490
Other emojis include T.J. Miller, Jennifer
Coolidge, Ilana Glazer, Maya Rudolph, and

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:50.490
James Corden.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:56.660
Oh, and don't forget Patrick Stewart playing
the illustrious role of Poop.

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:57.940
"Hahaha.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:59.210
Hahahaha!

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:00.580
No!

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:01.760
No!

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.040
NO!"

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:08.290
Honestly, that's enough reason to see this
thing on opening day: July 28th.

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.529
The Dark Tower

00:10:09.529 --> 00:10:15.480
This eagerly anticipated adaptation-slash-continuation
of the Stephen King book series stars Idris

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:20.460
Elba as The Gunslinger and Matthew McConaughey
as The Man in Black, arch-enemies battling

00:10:20.460 --> 00:10:22.649
through an Old West dystopia.

00:10:22.649 --> 00:10:28.180
Not exactly following the books, The Dark
Tower sees The Gunslinger searching for, well,

00:10:28.180 --> 00:10:31.839
the Dark Tower in order to give life back
to his land.

00:10:31.839 --> 00:10:36.000
After a delay to complete the film's visual
effects, The Dark Tower will be premiering

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:37.640
on August 4th.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:39.370
Annabelle: Creation

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:43.340
She's the creepiest doll since Chucky… and
whatever this thing is.

00:10:44.800 --> 00:10:50.300
"Hahahahahahahahahahaha-ahhahahahaha"

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:54.949
This summer, Annabelle is back to haunt your
dreams, and now, we get to meet Annabelle's

00:10:54.949 --> 00:10:57.470
makers, who are probably totally nice people.

00:10:57.470 --> 00:11:01.790
Of course, all of the fun starts after they
take in a nun and a group of children after

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:03.459
their orphanage closes down.

00:11:03.459 --> 00:11:05.600
Surely, nothing bad will happen to them.

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:10.120
In a summer with very few horror films, make
sure to check out this sequel on August 11th

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.769
to get your fright fix.

00:11:11.769 --> 00:11:13.520
The Hitman's Bodyguard

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:18.029
It's a tale as old as time: the best bodyguard
in the world has to keep a hit man safe so

00:11:18.029 --> 00:11:21.589
he can testify at the International Court
of Justice.

00:11:21.589 --> 00:11:25.120
They also have to bring down a murderous dictator
and somehow try to get along.

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:27.000
They're like the original odd couple.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:30.070
"Ba duh ba-doo ba-dooo!

00:11:30.070 --> 00:11:31.610
Buh-bu-duh duh-bu-duh...duh…"

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:36.360
Ryan Reynolds, Gary Oldman, and Samuel L.
Jackson make this international intrigue action

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:38.279
film look like a late summer winner.

00:11:38.279 --> 00:11:42.660
Don't get whacked until at least August 18th
if you want to check this one out.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:43.660
Polaroid

00:11:43.660 --> 00:11:48.920
Norwegian director Lars Klevberg builds upon
his 2015 short film of the same name with

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:53.259
Polaroid, which promises to creep your pants
off on August 25th.

00:11:53.259 --> 00:11:58.060
Starring Riverdale's Madelaine Petsch, Finding
Carter's Kathryn Prescott, and X-Files alum

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:03.040
Mitch Pileggi, the story centers on an outcast
teen who finds a vintage Polaroid camera with

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:06.960
some kind of terrible curse, since all the
people who get their pictures taken come to

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:08.350
a horrible end.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:12.740
If it's anything like the original short,
you'll never want to say cheese again.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:16.750
"Hey mouse, seh cheeese."

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:20.990
Thanks for watching!

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:23.410
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:25.589
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

